            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "## Task: Generate a forest plot comparing cross-lingual transfer asymmetry between Conflict and XNLI tasks\n\nWrite a Python matplotlib script and execute it to generate a forest plot.\n\n**Output paths:**\n- PDF: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-prod42/projects/clkc_mech_interp/figures/paper/fig3_asymmetry_forest.pdf`\n- PNG: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-prod42/projects/clkc_mech_interp/figures/paper/fig3_asymmetry_forest.png`\n\nThe directory exists at `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-prod42/projects/clkc_mech_interp/figures/paper/`\n\n**Data (transfer asymmetry = acc(ZH→EN) - acc(EN→ZH), in percentage points):**\n\n| Row Label | Point Estimate (pp) | CI Lower | CI Upper | Task |\n|-----------|-------------------|----------|----------|------|\n| Llama-3.1-8B (Conflict) | +7.22 | +1.10 | +13.61 | conflict |\n| Llama-3.1-8B (XNLI) | +5.97 | +0.92 | +11.33 | xnli |\n| Qwen3-8B (Conflict) | +7.18 | -1.19 | +13.41 | conflict |\n| Qwen3-8B (XNLI) | +6.72 | +2.36 | +11.73 | xnli |\n\n**narrative_intent:**\n\"The transfer asymmetry (ZH→EN > EN→ZH) in knowledge conflict detection matches that of the non-conflict XNLI baseline in magnitude — CIs overlap substantially — demonstrating that asymmetry is a general cross-lingual property of English-dominant models, not conflict-specific.\"\n\n**Design requirements (Pattern L forest plot):**\n\n1. **Layout**: 3-column structure using GridSpec\n   - Left column (width ratio ~2): Row labels (model + task type)\n   - Center column (width ratio ~4): CI interval plot (dot + horizontal line)\n   - Right column (width ratio ~2): Inline numbers: \"Δ [CI_lo, CI_hi] pp\"\n\n2. **Reference elements:**\n   - Vertical dashed black line at x=0 (no asymmetry)\n   - Semi-transparent gray band from -2 to +2 pp (equivalence zone) with \"±2pp\" label\n   - x-axis labeled \"Transfer Asymmetry (ZH→EN − EN→ZH), pp\"\n\n3. **Color semantic:**\n   - Conflict rows: vermillion (#D55E00), solid circle marker, size=8\n   - XNLI rows: blue (#0072B2), solid circle marker, size=8\n   - CI lines: same color as dots, linewidth=2\n\n4. **Row grouping:**\n   - Group by model: Llama rows together (top), Qwen rows together (bottom)\n   - Light horizontal separator or subtle background alternation between model groups\n   - Row spacing: ~0.8 between rows within group, ~1.5 between groups\n\n5. **Style:**\n   - figsize=(7, 3)\n   - Font: DejaVu Sans, label text 10pt, inline numbers 9pt\n   - No top/right spines on center panel; left panel has no spines\n   - savefig.bbox='tight', DPI=300\n   - PDF vector + PNG\n   - The center panel x-axis should range from about -4 to +16 to show all CIs comfortably\n   - Add a small legend in the top-right corner: \"● Conflict  ● XNLI\" with the two colors\n\n6. **Key visual emphasis:**\n   - The substantial CI overlap between Conflict and XNLI rows within each model group is THE key message\n   - Consider adding light vertical shaded regions or connecting brackets to emphasize overlap (optional, only if clean)\n\nAfter writing the script, execute it and verify both PDF and PNG exist and are non-empty.\n"
            }
          ],
